      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Idiomaticity - No Magic Values in Boundary Tests:**\n\nThe offsets `0x1000` and `0x50000` are magic numbers. Boundary test cases must derive from the named constant under test rather than hardcoding raw numbers.\n\nInstead of arbitrary addresses, derive the exact offsets relative to the boundary (`CONFIG_WP_STORAGE_SIZE`), which enforces the invariant programmatically.\n\n```c\n\t/* Writes into the protected region are rejected... */\n\tzassert_equal(cros_flash_physical_write(cros_flash_dev, CONFIG_WP_STORAGE_SIZE - sizeof(value),\n\t\t\t\t\t\tsizeof(value),\n\t\t\t\t\t\t(const char *)\u0026value),\n\t\t      EC_ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED);\n\n\t/* ...writes outside of it are allowed. */\n\tzassert_equal(cros_flash_physical_write(cros_flash_dev, CONFIG_WP_STORAGE_SIZE,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tsizeof(value),\n\t\t\t\t\t\t(const char *)\u0026value),\n\t\t      EC_SUCCESS);\n```\n\nAlso applies to the magic numbers used in other tests:\n* **Line 411:** `0x70000` in `test_protect_now_all` (consider using `FAKE_FLASH_SIZE - sizeof(value)`)\n* **Line 463:** `0x20000` in `test_write_erase_roundtrip` (consider using `0` or defining a `TEST_OFFSET` constant) [🔗](http://go/tj/3fe6a065-8c59-4ad6-8ed9-a62f4178cab0)",
